h) VM Performance Troubleshooting

Practiced basic troubleshooting when the Ubuntu VM became slow.

Checked CPU, memory, disk space, and running processes using:

free -h
top
df -h
ps aux

Based on the resource usage, performed basic corrective actions such as stopping unnecessary processes/services and checking the VM's CPU and RAM allocation in VMware.

Troubleshooting Approach
VM became slow
      ↓
Check RAM → free -h
      ↓
Check CPU/processes → top / ps aux
      ↓
Check disk space → df -h
      ↓
Check VMware CPU/RAM allocation
      ↓
Stop unnecessary process/service if required
      ↓
Re-check system performance

